  "packageSize": 226266,
  "published": "2026-11-17T11:37:10.063Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 0.0.5\n\nBuilt against `sdk_ui` 0.0.61 (Halo SDK 4.0.28).\n\n- The package is now pinned to work with `Microsoft.Maui.Controls` 10.0.0 or later, so any .NET 10 MAUI app can use it.\n\n## 0.0.4\n\nBuilt against `sdk_ui` 0.0.61 (Halo SDK 4.0.28).\n\n- The AWS session token is marked optional, since it's only needed for temporary credentials.\n\n## 0.0.3\n\nBuilt against `sdk_ui` 0.0.61 (Halo SDK 4.0.28). No API change for hosts.\n\n- A fresh install's first start no longer fails with `FAILED_VALIDATE`: registration waits until the merchant has answered the permission prompt.\n- If the merchant refuses while an SDK screen is up, the SDK holds on a permissions page with **Allow access** and **Open settings**, and carries on once everything is granted.\n- If they refuse during `InitAsync`, it returns `ErrorCode = \"PermissionsNotGranted\"` and `ErrorSettings = \"APP\"`, so the host can show its own permission screen. Calling `InitAsync` again asks again.\n\n## 0.0.2\n\nUpdated README \n\n- The README's Quick start now shows how each can run\n\n## 0.0.1\n\nInitial release, built against `sdk_ui` 0.0.60 (Halo SDK 4.0.28).\n\n- Tap-on-phone payments and card-present refunds through the SDK's own screens\n- Printing, receipts and Zebra printer pairing\n- Branding through `brand.json`",
